# The log is borrowed to read: `note` clones its lines (a library operation whose result it names) and pushes the line
# onto the copy, which it drops. It gives nothing back and changes nothing, the arrow into the terminal object. `run`
# counts the lines of the log as it built it.
route journal.run
step run/Log()
step run/note
step run/note/clone
step run/note/push

line entry > run call
line run/Log() > Log·log@run/Log() value
line Log·log@run/Log() > run/note/clone value
line run/note/clone > _·lines@run/note/clone value
line _·lines@run/note/clone > run/note/push value
line run/note/push > _·lines@run/note/push value
line Log·log@run/Log() > run value

home Log·log@run/Log() run
home _·lines@run/note/clone run/note
home _·lines@run/note/push run/note

side entry left
